@startuml Sandbox Environment Setup Sequence

!theme plain
title SABER Docker Sandbox Environment Setup - Actual Implementation

actor Agent
participant "SessionManager" as SM
participant "BenchmarkManager" as BM
participant "EpisodeManager" as EM_EP
participant "ExecutionManager" as EM
participant "EnvironmentLoader" as EL
participant "SandboxEnvironmentManager" as SBMGR
participant "PermanentEnvironmentManager" as PMGR
participant "DockerSandboxEnvironment" as DSE
participant "Docker Compose" as DC

== Episode Initialization (Actual Flow) ==

Agent -> SM: POST /session/{id}/start-episode?task_id=dvwa_sql_injection
activate SM

SM -> BM: get_task(task_id)
activate BM

BM --> SM: Task (with environment, execution_config, episode_config)
deactivate BM

SM -> EM_EP: start_episode(session_id, task_id, initial_context)
activate EM_EP

EM_EP -> EM_EP: create Episode object (state=ACTIVE)
EM_EP --> SM: Episode
deactivate EM_EP

== Task Configuration and Environment Setup ==

SM -> EM: configure_for_task(session_id, task)
activate EM

note over EM
ExecutionManager configures from task object:
- Resolves task.environment via EnvironmentLoader
- Creates/updates SandboxEnvironmentManager
- Configures ExecutorFactory with task config
- No complex permanent environment coordination
end note

EM -> EL: resolve_environment(task.environment)
activate EL

note over EL
EnvironmentLoader handles:
- Template reference (string → SandboxEnvironmentSpec)
- Granular config (dict → SandboxEnvironmentSpec)
- Hybrid template + additions
- Network configuration
end note

EL --> EM: SandboxEnvironmentSpec
deactivate EL

EM -> EM: update _sandbox_manager with resolved environment
EM -> EM: update _configuration with task.execution_config
EM --> SM: configuration_complete
deactivate EM

== Additional Component Configuration ==

SM -> SM: policy_manager.configure_for_task(session_id, task)
SM -> SM: episode_manager.configure_for_task(session_id, task)
SM -> SM: update session (current_episode_id, current_task_id)

SM --> Agent: {episode_id, task_id, session_id, message}
deactivate SM

== Command Execution with Lazy Environment Creation ==

Agent -> SM: MCP tool call: cli(command="nmap dvwa_webapp")
activate SM

SM -> EM: execute_action(session_id, action)
activate EM

EM -> SBMGR: get_session_environment(session_id)
activate SBMGR

alt Environment not yet created
    SBMGR -> SBMGR: create_session_environment(session_id, environment_spec)
    SBMGR -> DSE: new DockerSandboxEnvironment(session_id, environment_spec)
    activate DSE

    note over DSE
    Environment creation happens on first command:
    - Generate Docker Compose configuration
    - Start all required services (execution + targets)
    - Wait for health checks
    - Set up networking
    end note

    DSE -> DC: docker-compose up -d
    activate DC

    DC -> DC: Start execution container + target services
    DC -> DC: Wait for all health checks
    DC --> DSE: All services healthy
    deactivate DC

    DSE -> DSE: verify_environment_health()
    DSE --> SBMGR: DockerSandboxEnvironment ready
    deactivate DSE
else Environment already exists
    SBMGR --> SBMGR: return existing environment
end

SBMGR --> EM: DockerSandboxEnvironment
deactivate SBMGR

EM -> DSE: execute_command(["nmap", "dvwa_webapp"])
activate DSE

note over DSE
Command executes in execution container
with network access to target services
via Docker Compose internal networking
end note

DSE -> DSE: run_in_execution_container()
DSE --> EM: CommandResult(success=True, data="Host dvwa_webapp is up...")
deactivate DSE

EM --> SM: CommandResult
deactivate EM

SM --> Agent: MCP result with nmap output
deactivate SM

== Optional: Permanent Environment Integration ==

note over PMGR
Permanent Environment Manager is optional:
- Initialized separately via initialize_permanent_environment_manager()
- Provides persistent services across episodes
- Sandbox environments can connect to permanent networks
- Not required for basic sandbox functionality
end note

== Environment Cleanup ==

Agent -> SM: DELETE /session/{id}
activate SM

SM -> EM: cleanup_session(session_id)
activate EM

EM -> SBMGR: cleanup_session(session_id)
activate SBMGR

SBMGR -> DSE: stop()
activate DSE

DSE -> DC: docker-compose down --volumes
activate DC

DC -> DC: Stop and remove all containers, networks, volumes
DC --> DSE: Environment cleaned up
deactivate DC

DSE --> SBMGR: Cleanup complete
deactivate DSE

SBMGR --> EM: Session cleaned up
deactivate SBMGR

EM --> SM: Cleanup complete
deactivate EM

SM --> Agent: 200 OK - Session terminated
deactivate SM

note over Agent, DC
**Actual Sandbox Environment Implementation**

**Key Architecture Principles:**
- Lazy environment creation: Sandbox created on first command execution
- Simple task-based configuration via task.environment
- Docker Compose orchestration for all environments (single or multi-container)
- Optional permanent environment integration
- Session-scoped environment lifecycle

**Environment Resolution:**
- task.environment can be string template reference or dict config
- EnvironmentLoader resolves to SandboxEnvironmentSpec
- SandboxEnvironmentManager creates DockerSandboxEnvironment
- Docker Compose handles all container orchestration

**Execution Flow:**
1. Episode starts with task configuration
2. ExecutionManager configures from task object
3. Environment creation deferred until first command
4. Commands execute in dedicated execution container
5. Target services available via Docker Compose networking
6. Complete cleanup on session termination

**No Complex Orchestration:**
- No benchmark session management
- No complex permanent/ephemeral coordination during episode start
- Simple REST endpoint: POST /session/{id}/start-episode
- Client-side benchmark orchestration
end note

@enduml
